    if [file], creates, [predicate]
    and [other file], creates, [predicate]
    and [other file], differs from, [file]

a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: a fake, returned, file, nowhere"
a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, must break, Each predicate has one creator

a spec that looks for itself, adds line, spec.plain, "ghost.txt, is, in the folder"
a spec that looks for itself, must break, Each predicate has one creator

a workflow that makes up a result, adds line, workflow.plain, "a comment, broke, The only knowledge is Datalog"
a workflow that makes up a result, must break, Each predicate has one creator

"engine.go, loads, spec.plain", means in mangle, 'loads("engine.go", "spec.plain").'
"spec.plain, is, in the folder", means in mangle, in_the_folder("spec.plain").
a law is broken, means in mangle, a_law_is_broken().
"[any file], is, a used file", means in mangle, a_used_file(AnyFile).
"true, exits with, 0", means in mangle, 'exits_with("true", 0).'
'a change, adds line, notes.plain, "a, is, a note"', means in mangle, 'adds_line("a change", "notes.plain", "a, is, a note").'
"[file], ends with, [ending]", means in mangle, ":string:ends_with(File, Ending)"
"[command], starts with, [prefix]", means in mangle, ":string:starts_with(Command, Prefix)"
"[file], differs from, [other file]", means in mangle, File != OtherFile
'[command], is the join of, "command: find the comments in ", [file]', means in mangle, 'Command = fn:string:concat("command: find the comments in ", File)'

[rule], breaks, Every rule reads back as written
    if [rule], is, read back differently

a rule that reads back differently, adds line, spec.plain, "engine.go, loads, extra.plain"
a rule that reads back differently, adds line, extra.plain, '"zzz", means, nothing'
a rule that reads back differently, must break, Every rule reads back as written
a rule that reads back differently, must explain, '"extra.plain:1, breaks, Every rule reads back as written", holds because, "extra.plain:1, is, read back differently"'

.plain, means, plain language
